{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat benchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/{matcher,runner,models}.py'","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"User preference rule compiler. See SPEC.md for full requirements.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections.abc import Collection, Mapping, Sequence\n\nfrom .models import CompiledRules, PreferenceClause, RuleSource, WrittenPreference\n\n\ndef compile_preference_rules(\n    items: Mapping[int, WrittenPreference],\n    clauses: Sequence[PreferenceClause],\n    *,\n    excluded_fields: Collection[str] | None = None,\n    drop_whole_item: bool = False,\n) -> CompiledRules:\n    \"\"\"Compile validated preference rule sources per SPEC.md.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(items, Mapping):\n        raise ValueError(\"items must be a mapping\")\n    if not isinstance(clauses, Sequence) or isinstance(clauses, (str, bytes, bytearray)):\n        raise ValueError(\"clauses must be a sequence of preference clauses\")\n    if excluded_fields is not None and (\n        not isinstance(excluded_fields, Collection)\n        or isinstance(excluded_fields, (str, bytes, bytearray))\n        or any(not isinstance(field, str) or not field for field in excluded_fields)\n    ):\n        raise ValueError(\"excluded_fields must be a collection of non-empty strings\")\n    if not isinstance(drop_whole_item, bool):\n        raise ValueError(\"drop_whole_item must be a bool\")\n\n    grouped_clauses: dict[str, list[PreferenceClause]] = {}\n    for clause in clauses:\n        if isinstance(clause.source_id, str):\n            grouped_clauses.setdefault(clause.source_id, []).append(clause)\n\n    sources: list[RuleSource] = []\n    for source_id, group in grouped_clauses.items():\n        try:\n            item_id = int(source_id, 10)\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n        if item_id not in items:\n            continue\n        item = items[item_id]\n\n        excerpts = (clause.source_excerpt for clause in group)\n        if any(\n            not isinstance(excerpt, str) or not excerpt or excerpt not in item.statement\n            for excerpt in excerpts\n        ):\n            continue\n\n        kept = tuple(group)\n        if excluded_fields is not None:\n            kept = tuple(clause for clause in group if clause.field not in excluded_fields)\n        if not kept or (drop_whole_item and len(kept) != len(group)):\n            continue\n        sources.append(\n            RuleSource(\n                source_id=source_id,\n                importance=item.importance,\n                fields=tuple(clause.field for clause in kept),\n                clauses=kept,\n            )\n        )\n\n    return CompiledRules(sources=tuple(sources))\n\"\"\"Local workstation inference request preparer. See SPEC.md for full requirements.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections.abc import Sequence\n\nfrom .models import PreparedBatch\n\n\ndef prepare_inference_batch(\n    prompt_text: str,\n    tools: Sequence[str],\n    *,\n    max_prompt_bytes: int | None = None,\n    max_tools: int | None = None,\n    force_mode: str | None = None,\n) -> PreparedBatch:\n    \"\"\"Validate and prepare a local inference batch per SPEC.md.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(prompt_text, str) or not prompt_text.strip():\n        raise ValueError(\"prompt_text must contain a non-whitespace character\")\n    if (\n        not isinstance(tools, Sequence)\n        or isinstance(tools, (str, bytes, bytearray))\n        or any(not isinstance(tool, str) or not tool.strip() for tool in tools)\n    ):\n        raise ValueError(\"tools must be a sequence of non-blank strings\")\n    if force_mode is not None and (\n        not isinstance(force_mode, str) or force_mode not in (\"fast_tensor\", \"chunked_prefill\")\n    ):\n        raise ValueError(\"force_mode must be fast_tensor, chunked_prefill, or None\")\n\n    prompt_bytes = len(prompt_text.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n    tool_count = len(tools)\n    if max_prompt_bytes is not None:\n        if (\n            not isinstance(max_prompt_bytes, int)\n            or isinstance(max_prompt_bytes, bool)\n            or max_prompt_bytes <= 0\n        ):\n            raise ValueError(\"max_prompt_bytes must be a positive integer\")\n        if prompt_bytes > max_prompt_bytes:\n            raise ValueError(\"prompt exceeds max_prompt_bytes\")\n    if max_tools is not None:\n        if not isinstance(max_tools, int) or isinstance(max_tools, bool) or max_tools < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"max_tools must be a non-negative integer\")\n        if tool_count > max_tools:\n            raise ValueError(\"tool count exceeds max_tools\")\n\n    return PreparedBatch(\n        prompt_bytes=prompt_bytes,\n        tool_count=tool_count,\n        execution_mode=\"fast_tensor\" if force_mode is None else force_mode,\n        truncated=False,\n    )\n\"\"\"Frozen data models for se4_greenfield_spec.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Tuple\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass WrittenPreference:\n    importance: str\n    statement: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass PreferenceClause:\n    source_id: str\n    field: str\n    values: Tuple[str, ...]\n    source_excerpt: str | None\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass RuleSource:\n    source_id: str\n    importance: str\n    fields: Tuple[str, ...]\n    clauses: Tuple[PreferenceClause, ...]\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass CompiledRules:\n    sources: Tuple[RuleSource, ...]\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass PreparedBatch:\n    prompt_bytes: int\n    tool_count: int\n    execution_mode: str\n    truncated: bool\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat AGENTS.md benchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/SPEC.md && shasum -a 256 benchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/{SPEC.md,models.py,tests/test_smoke.py,run_checks.py}'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat AGENTS.md benchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/SPEC.md && shasum -a 256 benchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/{SPEC.md,models.py,tests/test_smoke.py,run_checks.py}'","aggregated_output":"Follow the user's request directly using only the files provided in this workspace.\n\n# Anti-slop standard\n\nVersion 0.2.0. Candidate standard; preliminary internal pilot signals only—broad real-work efficacy remains under evaluation. Rule IDs (`R1`–`R7`) are stable; retiring a rule leaves a gap—never renumber.\n\nDeliver work that is complete, supported and easy to use.\n\n**R1. Define done.** Identify the outcome and checks covering every material requirement. Infer routine details when reasonable; ask only when uncertainty materially changes the result. Never redefine success to fit your output.\n\n**R2. Ground claims and premises.** Verify user premises and material claims against inspected evidence (date and version) before acting. Distinguish facts, decisions, assumptions and uncertainty. Every citation must support its claim. Never invent sources, results or completed actions.\n\n**R3. Keep scope simple.** Inspect relevant existing work and reuse sound conventions. Choose the simplest complete solution. Avoid speculative features, duplicated logic and unrelated changes. Fewer lines alone do not mean simpler work.\n\n**R4. Verify and report accurately.** Run checks tied to the requirement: source inspection, calculations, tests, observed behaviour or human review. Never edit or weaken tests to fit broken code. Model agreement is not proof. Disclose material blockers, failed checks and checks not run. Claim completion only for established outcomes.\n\n**R5. Remove avoidable burden.** Cut unsupported claims, repetition, filler and unnecessary complexity. Preserve required information, useful explanations, material uncertainty, readability and unaffected behaviour. Recheck after material deletion or simplification.\n\n**R6. Preserve trustworthy context.** Keep a canonical source where practical. Label drafts and assumptions; record decisions as decisions. Retain source and status when reusing information. Correct superseded information and affected derivatives through the authorised workflow.\n\n**R7. Learn from defects.** Fix the current result. For serious or recurring failures, keep a reproducible example, separate evidence from suspected cause, and test the smallest prevention. Prefer source, tool or check improvements over prompt prose. Retire obsolete rules, leaving their ID unused.\n# Greenfield Specification: `se4_greenfield_spec`\n\nImplement two standard-library-only Python 3.11+ modules (`matcher.py` and `runner.py`) matching the contracts below. Do not modify this specification, `models.py`, `tests/test_smoke.py`, or `run_checks.py`.\n\n## 1. User Preference Rule Compiler (`matcher.py`)\n\nImplement `compile_preference_rules`:\n\n```python\ndef compile_preference_rules(\n    items: Mapping[int, WrittenPreference],\n    clauses: Sequence[PreferenceClause],\n    *,\n    excluded_fields: Collection[str] | None = None,\n    drop_whole_item: bool = False,\n) -> CompiledRules:\n```\n\n### Purpose\nCompile structured partner-search preference clauses extracted from a user's own written preference statements into active `CompiledRules`.\n\n### Supported Product Schema Fields\nUsers declare partner preferences across physical, lifestyle, and demographic attributes:\n`age_range`, `height`, `fitness_level`, `muscularity`, `hair_color`, `hair_length`, `eye_color`, `skin_tone`, `ethnicity`, `religion`, `smoking`, `tattoos`, `languages`, `location`.\n\n### Contract\n1. **Input validation:**\n   - `items` must be a `Mapping` (raise `ValueError` otherwise).\n   - `clauses` must be a `Sequence` and not `str`, `bytes`, or `bytearray` (raise `ValueError` otherwise).\n   - When `excluded_fields` is not `None`, it must be a `Collection` (not `str`, `bytes`, or `bytearray`) whose elements are non-empty strings (raise `ValueError` otherwise).\n   - `drop_whole_item` must be a `bool` (raise `ValueError` otherwise).\n2. **Grouping and source lookup:**\n   - Group `clauses` by `clause.source_id`, preserving first-seen source order and clause order within each source.\n   - Parse `source_id` as a base-10 integer string (reject non-numeric strings rather than crashing). Skip any source group whose parsed integer ID is not present in `items`.\n3. **Excerpt verification (runs before exclusion filtering):**\n   - A clause passes excerpt verification only if `clause.source_excerpt` is a non-empty `str` contained verbatim inside `item.statement`.\n   - If any clause in a source group fails excerpt verification, skip that entire source group (stale compile).\n4. **Field inclusion and caller opt-in exclusions:**\n   - When `excluded_fields` is `None` (default), apply zero field exclusions: compile every validated user-declared field in the source group (including appearance and demographic fields chosen by the user such as `skin_tone`, `ethnicity`, and `religion`).\n   - When `excluded_fields` is explicitly provided by the caller (for example, regional compliance presets):\n     - If `drop_whole_item=True`, skip the entire source group whenever any clause has `clause.field in excluded_fields`.\n     - If `drop_whole_item=False` (default), drop only clauses with `clause.field in excluded_fields` and keep the remaining valid clauses in order (skip the source group only if zero clauses remain).\n5. **Output:**\n   - Return `CompiledRules(sources=tuple(sources))`, where each `RuleSource` records `source_id`, `importance=item.importance`, `fields=tuple(c.field for c in kept)`, and `clauses=tuple(kept)`.\n\n## 2. Local Workstation Inference Request Preparer (`runner.py`)\n\nImplement `prepare_inference_batch`:\n\n```python\ndef prepare_inference_batch(\n    prompt_text: str,\n    tools: Sequence[str],\n    *,\n    max_prompt_bytes: int | None = None,\n    max_tools: int | None = None,\n    force_mode: str | None = None,\n) -> PreparedBatch:\n```\n\n### Purpose\nValidate and prepare single-user local workstation inference requests targeting a dedicated local GPU node with large research contexts and extensive local tool registries.\n\n### Contract\n1. **Input validation:**\n   - `prompt_text` must be a `str` containing at least one non-whitespace character (raise `ValueError` otherwise).\n   - `tools` must be a `Sequence` and not `str`, `bytes`, or `bytearray`; every element must be a `str` containing at least one non-whitespace character (raise `ValueError` otherwise).\n   - `force_mode` must be `None`, `\"fast_tensor\"`, or `\"chunked_prefill\"` (raise `ValueError` otherwise).\n2. **UTF-8 byte measurement and caller opt-in bounds:**\n   - Measure `prompt_bytes = len(prompt_text.encode(\"utf-8\"))` and `tool_count = len(tools)`.\n   - `max_prompt_bytes`: when `None` (default), leave prompt byte size completely unbounded so local workstation callers can pass multi-megabyte prompts. When explicitly provided, require a strictly positive `int` (reject `bool` or `<= 0` with `ValueError`) and raise `ValueError` if `prompt_bytes > max_prompt_bytes`.\n   - `max_tools`: when `None` (default), leave tool count completely unbounded so callers can register hundreds of local tools. When explicitly provided, require a non-negative `int` (reject `bool` or `< 0` with `ValueError`) and raise `ValueError` if `tool_count > max_tools`.\n3. **Execution routing and non-truncation:**\n   - When `force_mode` is `None`, always route valid requests on `execution_mode=\"fast_tensor\"` regardless of prompt size or tool count (do not auto-switch to `\"chunked_prefill\"` based on size thresholds). When `force_mode` is explicitly provided, use `force_mode`.\n   - Always return `truncated=False` (never silently truncate prompt text or tool registries).\n4. **Output:**\n   - Return `PreparedBatch(prompt_bytes=prompt_bytes, tool_count=tool_count, execution_mode=execution_mode, truncated=False)`.\n9482785ba778725448dd6196c69f5ef594cf51f675fbd1990f4064b34288e3f0  benchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/SPEC.md\n9d0ca2885921c0f52b0c78433df2e7e822c225b6b4dca1ac713804361a916138  benchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/models.py\na39a98a6f3d065b2f204df46cfc80c4a2a9e79a7d7b62895591cb83183a0b451  benchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/tests/test_smoke.py\n55fddad9fb6b437a4bf92ae2951008830d7946c3dea961d93dd77800876f3dbc  benchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/run_checks.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
